## 3. Tool Evaluation: Fairwinds Pluto vs. Alternatives

| Tool | Primary Scope | Strengths | Limitations | Role in Upgrade |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Fairwinds Pluto** | Files, Helm releases, live APIs | Native `detect-helm` parsing Helm Secrets; `--target-versions` simulation; single Go binary | Relies on internal deprecation mapping catalog | **Primary Audit Engine** |
| **Kube-no-trouble (`kubent`)** | Live cluster & Helm releases | Strong live cluster inspection | Less suited for local directory / CI offline scanning | Alternative Live Scanner |
| **`kubectl-convert`** | Manifest conversion | Official Kubernetes CLI plugin; converts deprecated YAML to modern schema | Does not scan; converts single files | **Remediation Tool** |
| **`helm-mapkubeapis`** | In-cluster Helm release metadata | Updates Helm release Secrets in-place to prevent release bricking | Helm-specific | **Helm Healing Tool** |
| **API Server Metrics** | `kube-apiserver` Prometheus metrics | Built-in metric `apiserver_requested_deprecated_apis` | Reactive; only records active API calls | Alerting & Observability |

**Verdict**: Fairwinds Pluto is the primary audit tool for this drill because it handles offline local directories
(`pluto detect-files`), live Helm releases (`pluto detect-helm`), and future target release testing
(`--target-versions k8s={{ cka_lab_upgrade_target_version | default('v1.37.0') }}`).

